# tools/ales_album_diff_witness.rish — what changed between two record versions: classify(before, after) sorts every track into
# added, removed, changed, or same (ALES232).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES232.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-144541_fill-ales232-lotus-album-diff.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/library_diff.rye (ALES229, the classification one level up) · lotus/album_find.rye (ALES231, the resolve this
# composes on) · lotus/album_manifest.rye (ALES224, the two opened records this compares). A read — no new frame, no new hash, no
# error union.
#
# lotus/album_diff.rye classifies two opened album manifests, a before and an after. The selftest proves: an after-only track appears
# once as added with its digest (the added law); a before-only track appears once as removed with its digest (the removed law); a name
# in both with a moved digest appears once as changed carrying old and new, an unchanged name in no list and counted same (the changed
# law); a record against itself yields all zeros and same_count equal to the track count (the identity law). A pure classification —
# no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_album_diff_witness.rish

say "ales-album-diff: Language EN — ALES232 classifies two record versions (a before and an after album manifest) into added, removed, changed, and same — the honest answer to what changed in this record since the last master."
say "ales-album-diff: Style Radiant — a diff composes on the ALES231 resolve rather than re-walking from scratch; the content-address digest IS the whole comparison (no byte compare, no new hash), mirroring library_diff (ALES229) one level down; the added law, the removed law, the changed law, and the identity law each proven on metal."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/album_diff"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/album_diff.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-album-diff: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/album_diff.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-album-diff: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-album-diff: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-album-diff' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-album-diff: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-album-diff line"

say "ales-album-diff: GREEN — a keeper sees what moved in a record between two masters now, and the album level carries its own second-order primitive at parity with the library level. The next Lotus crux still names who made it — a signed carry (crypto seam) on Keaton's word."
